.TH CONFSTR 3 "September 20, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
confstr \- return a DiscoBSD configuration string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B size_t confstr(int name, char *buffer, size_t length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Confstr
supports
.B _CS_PATH
and returns the required buffer size, including the terminating null byte,
for the standard utility path
.BR /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin .
.PP
A zero
.I length
or a null
.I buffer
performs a size query.  A short buffer receives as much of the path as fits
and always ends with a null byte.
.PP
An unsupported selector returns zero, sets
.I errno
to
.BR EINVAL ,
and leaves the output buffer unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
paths(3), sysconf(3)
